    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d331">

                <pb facs="d331-01" n="1" xml:id="d331-01"/>

                <head>331. Telegram 5090 From the Embassy in Afghanistan to the Department of
                        State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d331-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d331-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName>Kabul</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1969-10-06T11:50:00+00:00">October 6, 1969, 1150Z</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>Conte Amendment</p>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>Ref:</head>
                    <item>Kabul 4515</item>
                </list>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>At first opportunity since Farhadi’s return from Rabat conference, I
                        called on him Oct. 5 and noted that month had elapsed since my previous
                        approach concerning acquisition SU-7 aircraft (reftel).</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>He said that following my earlier call he had discussed matter with King,
                        PriMin and Min Def. Latter assured him that aircraft intended as replacement
                        aircraft for planes which either have crashed or older aircraft to be
                        removed from Afghan forces in view spiraling costs of maintenance. Min Def
                        also said all negotiations for SU-7s had been concluded before Jan. 2, 1968
                        and he would provide Farhadi all pertinent details in near future.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item> Farhadi told me he believes King and others realize seriousness of Conte
                        issue and fact that Embassy, as well as executive branch, had no option but
                        to investigate thoroughly and enforce law if facts so indicate. He,
                        therefore, expects full RGA cooperation although he has had some
                        difficulties with Pri Min who has appeared very concerned over question <pb
                            facs="d331-02" n="2" xml:id="d331-02"/> whether amendment constitutes
                        “condition” or political “string” to US aid.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>I expect to see King within next two weeks (he will be in southern
                        provinces until Oct 11) to follow up these preliminary steps at Fon Off
                        level.</item>
                </list>
                <closer>
                    <signed> Neumann </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d331-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d331-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files 1967–69, DEF 19–6 USSR–AFG.
                    Confidential.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d331-f2" n="2" xml:id="d331-f2-content">
                <p>Afghani Deputy Foreign Minister Farhadi assured Ambassador Neumann that the SU–7s
                    were purchased as replacement aircraft, and that the agreement to do so was
                    negotiated before January 2, 1968. Therefore, the Conte amendment should not
                    come into play.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
